 "summary": "A pair of PNP transistors made from neighbouring die of one wafer and sealed in a six-lead SOT363, each with its own base, collector and emitter brought out and nothing joining the two inside. Each transistor holds off -45 V collector to emitter and -50 V collector to base, and carries -100 mA steadily or -200 mA in a pulse. At -2 mA the current gain is 220 to 475, the two transistors agreeing to within 10 %, and their base-emitter voltages fall within 2 mV of each other. The whole package may turn 200 mW into heat at 25 °C ambient.",
