 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Matched pair",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The two transistors come from neighbouring die of a single wafer, so they track each other. Their gains agree to within 10 % and their base-emitter voltages to within 2 mV, both measured at VCE = -5 V and IC = -2 mA. Each transistor keeps its own base, collector and emitter, and the two share no node inside the package."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal rating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 200 mW dissipation and the 625 °C/W junction-to-ambient figures cover both transistors together, for a part soldered to the suggested pad layout in 1 oz copper on a single-sided 1.6 mm FR4 board, in still air and at thermal equilibrium. Above about 25 °C ambient, what the package may dissipate falls in a straight line as the temperature rises."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Measurement",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Each electrical figure is taken with a pulse short enough to keep the junction from warming while it is measured."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Automotive grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Diodes Incorporated makes automotive grades under specific change control. Those parts carry AEC-Q100, AEC-Q101, AEC-Q104 or AEC-Q200 qualification, support PPAP, and are built in plants certified to IATF 16949."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Materials",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "No lead is added, and the part meets EU directives 2002/95/EC, 2011/65/EU and 2015/863/EU. It is also halogen and antimony free, which Diodes Incorporated defines as under 900 ppm bromine, under 900 ppm chlorine, under 1500 ppm the two together, and under 1000 ppm antimony compounds."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each part carries M3W for the type, followed by two characters that give the year and the month it was made."
  }
 ],
